# Static files and add-on extraction

- `internal/staticfiles.Store` owns `datadir.Layout.Static()`. Names are allowlisted by `ValidateName` (no Windows device names, no trailing dot) and resolved inside the directory; invalid names are rejected, never rewritten. Never buffer whole uploads in memory; the HTTP handler streams multipart parts and reads the raw `filename` parameter (not `Part.FileName`, which strips directories).
- Limits (`Options`): total size quota (`--static-quota-mb`), `MaxFiles`, a free-space reserve on the file system (`free_*.go`, `golang.org/x/sys`), `UploadsPerKey` concurrent uploads (`BeginUpload`). All are checked against bytes actually received: `Stage` streams to `.upload-*` temp files and stops at the per-file limit, the quota budget or the reserve; `Commit` re-checks everything exactly under `commitMu` and then places files (rename over existing files after keeping a `.upload-replaced-*` hard link, hard link for new names), rolling back to the previous state on any failure. `Remove` takes the same lock. `Open` sweeps every `.upload-*` leftover (backups are extra links, so nothing is lost). `Usage` feeds the list response.
- `internal/extract.Zip(zipPath, tmpRoot, Limits)` is the only extractor (ZIP only, no tar). It first checks the archive's own records (`layout.go`: EOCD/zip64, central directory vs archive/zip, local header names equal central names, no overlapping entry spans, data descriptors accounted), then the central directory (entry count, sizes, ratios per entry, whole archive and against the real archive size via `ratioBudget`, depth, path length, unsafe or colliding names including case-insensitive collisions, non-regular entries), creates its own fresh `os.MkdirTemp` destination under `tmpRoot` (use `datadir.Layout.Tmp()`), masks modes to 0644/0755 and bounds bytes actually written. Never extract into an existing tree such as a repository checkout. Its caller is the build pipeline (`build.stageAddons`, per-build staging below `tmp/`, see the builds rule). A static file a project lists in `static_addons` cannot be deleted (`handleDeleteStatic` asks `store.ProjectsUsingStatic`).
- Verify with `go test ./internal/staticfiles/... ./internal/extract/...` (bombs, overlapping entries, traversal, modes, quota, rollback, concurrent and interrupted uploads are covered).
